00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:08.320 align:start position:0%
our vehicle is constructed from foam  with carbon fiber-reinforced wings it  has a single control surface at the tail  which is controlled by a hobby servo  motor for our experiment we will only  consider the aircraft's lateral planar  dynamics for tracking the aircraft's  position will use a vikon motion capture  studio we will define our perching  maneuver as the aircraft starting 3.5  meters from the perch at 7 meters per  second and landing in a six point five  centimeter capture region with less than  one meter per second of forward velocity  we demonstrate the robustness of our  system by throwing the glider by hand  landing on powerlines to recharge it  provides a unique opportunity to improve  the mission duration of unmanned aerial  vehicles in this project we explore  whether or not we can successfully perch  on a powerline with a fixed-wing UAV  using only the magnetic field generated  by the powerline to localize the  aircraft these results demonstrate the  magnetic field based estimates are  sufficient for achieving closed-loop  perching and could be a reliable means  of perching on power lines in the field  finally we take our powerline perching  glider outdoors and demonstrate that we  are able to perch successfully in  outdoor environments when wind is  limited
 

